{"schemaVersion":1,"seq":4,"prev":"7ad30f09a7b16e9602eb227062c1aea528239e0739fe9a29173878e4b7fc6a32","at":"2026-09-27T05:55:43.053985Z","type":"node_output","state":"discover","iter":0,"node":"discover","data":{"output":{"findings":[{"tag":"advisory","file":"cmd/metareview/main_test.go","start_line":1214,"end_line":1218,"issue":"The assertion `strings.Contains(errOut, \"mock\")` is always true for these fixtures: record-lenses prints `record-lenses: --from-run %q: %v`, and both run IDs (\"mockinit\", \"mocktainted\") contain \"mock\". Any exit-2 rejection passes — wrong diff, unreadable init, non-passing outcome, missing run — and the check cannot tell which new branch fired.","consequence":"If a fixture later broke, or the rejection came from another check, the test would still pass without proving the mock-init and mock-taint branches work. Match the specific messages or use run IDs that don't contain \"mock\".","confidence":90,"severity":"P3"},{"tag":"advisory","file":"cmd/metareview/main.go","start_line":778,"end_line":788,"issue":"The mock rejection runs only in record-lenses; the gate does not re-check a stored marker's FromFSMRunID. A subagent-adjudicated marker recorded under 0.13.4 from a mock run still satisfies pr-ready/task-done/epic-ready after upgrading while base..HEAD is unchanged.","consequence":"A gate already holding a marker from a mock run keeps passing until the next commit or base change invalidates it, and nothing tells upgraders.","confidence":60,"severity":"P3"}]}}}
{"schemaVersion":1,"seq":5,"prev":"a2c69430e9713b384038568530e64ce9850593035d6aff29ecf485a7144e415c","at":"2026-09-27T05:55:43.276333Z","type":"delta_applied","state":"discover","iter":0,"node":"discover","data":{"findings":[{"issue_text":"[ADVISORY] The assertion `strings.Contains(errOut, \"mock\")` is always true for these fixtures: record-lenses prints `record-lenses: --from-run %q: %v`, and both run IDs (\"mockinit\", \"mocktainted\") contain \"mock\". Any exit-2 rejection passes — wrong diff, unreadable init, non-passing outcome, missing run — and the check cannot tell which new branch fired. If a fixture later broke, or the rejection came from another check, the test would still pass without proving the mock-init and mock-taint branches work. Match the specific messages or use run IDs that don't contain \"mock\".","file":"cmd/metareview/main_test.go","line":1214,"severity":"p3","category":"advisory","source":"lens"},{"issue_text":"[ADVISORY] The mock rejection runs only in record-lenses; the gate does not re-check a stored marker's FromFSMRunID. A subagent-adjudicated marker recorded under 0.13.4 from a mock run still satisfies pr-ready/task-done/epic-ready after upgrading while base..HEAD is unchanged. A gate already holding a marker from a mock run keeps passing until the next commit or base change invalidates it, and nothing tells upgraders.","file":"cmd/metareview/main.go","line":778,"severity":"p3","category":"advisory","source":"lens"}],"output_hash":"987ae0df972972e9eaa9a0dc5e49ac920abf6c224602bdfea3e27480c8be423d"}}
